WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:08.900
What Hillsdale brings to Washington is a
deep understanding of principles that

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:13.580
principled statesmanship. I think that's
where the Kirby Center is going to be

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.810
focused, that's the people we are going to
develop and teach. We want to encourage

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:25.350
statesmen to be more ambitious and to
understand what, for example, are the

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:31.000
achievements of Washington and Lincoln
and Churchill to name three extremely

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:37.719
effective wielders of power who were
deeply devoted constitutional forms. It's

00:00:37.719 --> 00:00:40.289
important to teach about the
Constitution in the nation's capital for

00:00:40.289 --> 00:00:44.589
a very simple reason- it's supposed to be
the way they work things. Then the people

00:00:44.589 --> 00:00:47.299
who are actually running the government
will be reminded that there is this

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:51.880
document, it's written down, it's not that hard
to read, it wasn't intended to be hard to read.

00:00:51.889 --> 00:00:55.949
We are here in Washington D.C. to extend
the College's mission. We teach members of

00:00:55.949 --> 00:00:59.819
Congress on a regular basis. We talk to
them, we spend time with them, we help

00:00:59.819 --> 00:01:03.479
them write. We teach our students who
come from Hillsdale College. We teach

00:01:03.479 --> 00:01:06.940
congressional staff that come to our various
programs, the public that come to our

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:10.710
lectures. The Kirby Center and having it
right there on Capitol Hill for my own

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:15.470
self has helped me get my thinking
centered in the right place, so that I'm not

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:20.600
just talking about policies or not just
talking about politics, but thinking

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:25.030
about First Principles and how they have
to be reapplied to the problems of the

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:29.020
day so that we can resuscitate the
American idea. It's our first remote campus,

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:32.650
but its roots have to be in the mission
of the college because we don't do

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:34.240
anything that's not rooted it there,

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:39.159
and we thought of this as a way to teach
the constitutional forms and principles

00:01:39.159 --> 00:01:44.500
among the people who work under the
Constitution, and who also mostly have

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:47.979
forgotten what it means. If you can imagine
the early republic and people sitting

00:01:47.979 --> 00:01:50.590
around talking about how to make it work, they didn't have any idea, any precedent.

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:55.240
The Kirby Center is reintroducing
that. So for the Hillsdale idea and

00:01:55.240 --> 00:02:00.929
ideals to connect with Washington
political elites, proximity is key.

00:02:00.929 --> 00:02:03.670
Proximity is what the Kirby Center
provides Hillsdale College.

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:09.470
Hillsdale is a community of scholars who,
in a collegial atmosphere, want to work

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:14.290
together to pursue truth, beauty, and
goodness. I think it's not only educational

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:19.370
in the think-tank sense, but it's also a
place that develops people and develops

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:22.950
students and grows theminto people who can use a

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:26.580
very lofty education for practical purposes.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:32.700
There is that exciting element of young
people who are growing into adults who

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:36.600
want to do things with their lives. I
think that is the real spark of the place.

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:41.390
Architectures the ruling art. And the ruling art
means directing things toward its

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:46.880
purpose. We make our buildings and then
they make us. It's a very profound thing.

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:52.060
Think about that. You can say exactly
the same thing about a constitution.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:59.370
First we make it, then it makes us. We
wanted to respect the principles of form

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:03.190
and beauty that go along with the
building of America. It's a really

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:07.400
beautiful building. So, aesthetically it's
great. It really reminds me of Hillsdale.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:11.269
We always talk about the importance of
beautiful architecture and they really

00:03:11.269 --> 00:03:14.299
took that here. It sets the stage for
continuing that serious education.

00:03:14.299 --> 00:03:19.119
The classes and the internship were both quite demanding,

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:22.040
and learning how to be a good student, keep up with

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:26.470
my responsibilities here, but also do a
good job at my internship, and manage

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:29.930
networking and meeting with folks
afterwards. Sort of being able to do all that

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:33.280
at the same time and spin all those
plates was really valuable. Kirby Center

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:38.060
and Hillsdale College is helping guide us
back to that journey to we are what we

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:41.390
stand for and what made this country so
exceptional in the first place.

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:46.840
The people who who made the Kirby Center
happen-Mr. Kirby especially, but everyone

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:51.640
else who contributed to this place they
have done something that I think has changed

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:56.500
the conversation in Washington D.C. and
will continue to do so and will do so

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:03.489
more and more over time because of that
investment. Mr. Kirby is the leader of many, many

00:04:03.489 --> 00:04:07.209
people who've given money so we can do
this. I would say to them

00:04:07.209 --> 00:04:12.280
thank you most warmly. So far we have
done just what we hoped and we hope to

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:15.940
do yet more. And we're very grateful to you.

